<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-event-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Validate each emitted or stored event against the closed v2 schema and factory invariants. Reuse summarizeJobLifecycle over the proposed bounded ledger to enforce current event-key, logical-attempt, pairing, domain, UTC and arithmetic rules; do not duplicate or relax the reader. Exact canonical-content replay does not append again. A changed same-key record, conflicting terminal kind, changed logical/source/scope/tool/route/owner/domain relationship or malformed prior record refuses before mutation. Explicit null work/attempt/logical/source identities remain incomplete and unpairable. An incomplete start remains a fact, not success; replay cannot overwrite its clock domain or manufacture a terminal." <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-event-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-factory-shape> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "metrics-record-factory-shape" <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-factory-shape> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-factory-shape> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-factory-shape> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "createLifecycleObservation accepts one closed plain JSON object with exactly these required keys: eventKind, jobIdentity, jobType, issueIdentity, workIdentity, semanticOwnerIdentity, attemptIdentity, logicalAttemptIdentity, phaseIdentity, sourceIdentity, observedAt, clockDomainIdentity, startedAt, finishedAt, startOffsetNanoseconds, endOffsetNanoseconds, scopeIdentity, toolIdentity, routeIdentity. All enums, bounds and nullable identity meanings are inherited from the v2 event schema. Unknown values are explicit nulls, never omitted or inferred from CWD, PID, Git, argv, environment or a random identifier. No arbitrary missingness text, command, evidence, contribution, accepted outcome, cost, token, cache or outcome-lineage input is accepted. Set schema/clock/unit constants and compute eventKey from canonicalDigest({jobIdentity,workIdentity,attemptIdentity,phaseIdentity,eventKind}). Preserve actual canonical UTC instants separately from monotonic offsets; UTC reversal cannot change elapsed time." <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-factory-shape> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-locking-recovery> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "metrics-record-locking-recovery" <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-locking-recovery> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-locking-recovery> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-locking-recovery> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Use one recorder-specific .usf/locks/metrics-record.lock with the existing private-file and kernel flock trust pattern, never the Hermes activity/lifetime or primary integration lock. Only /usr/bin/flock with fixed exclusive/nonblock/conflict-exit-code75/fd3 arguments and env{} may acquire that lock; validate trusted executable identity/permissions and admitted root-UID mapping. Hold the parent-owned file descriptor through bounded read/validate/write/readback and release in finally; contention and unavailable tooling are explicit refusals, never spin or stale-owner deletion. Re-express the existing atomic private temporary-file plus fsync/rename/directory-fsync pattern under that lock, preserving named/opened identities before publication. Exact durable readback is required. On interruption, preserve the old complete ledger or the new complete ledger and let a later exact replay discover which; do not infer a terminal. Return only status appended/replayed, eventKey, raw ledger digest, byte and row counts; no authority effect." <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-locking-recovery> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-private-append> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "metrics-record-private-append" <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-private-append> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-private-append> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-private-append> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "appendLifecycleObservation accepts only one explicit canonical repository root and a valid factory event. Its only output ledger is .usf/metrics/job-lifecycle-v2.jsonl. Enforce canonical owner-controlled root, private .usf/metrics and .usf/locks directories, 0600 regular non-symlink single-link files and matching opened/named inode/device identity; refuse unsafe ancestors and changed paths. Limit each canonical UTF-8 event including newline to16384 bytes, complete ledger to8388608 bytes and100000 rows before allocation/parse/append. Refuse malformed or partial existing JSONL without deleting or truncating it. Never read raw session, credentials, provider homes or unrelated ledger files." <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-private-append> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-reported-outcomes> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "metrics-record-reported-outcomes" <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-reported-outcomes> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-reported-outcomes> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-reported-outcomes> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The factory always emits acceptedOutcome null, evidenceIdentity null, contributionDigest null, tokenFact/cacheFact/costFact null, parentAttemptIdentity null and overlapDisposition unknown. Start and finish have outcomeLineage null; failure and interrupted carry only their corresponding reported lifecycle lineage failed/interrupted, not observed semantic nonacceptance. For a start require null end/duration/finishedAt. For a terminal compute safe duration only when both nonnegative offsets are known and end>=start; otherwise retain null duration. intervals.total is that reported duration and all phase subintervals remain null. Use fixed bounded missingness text identifying unknown duration/acceptance/resource facts; never caller prose." <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
<urn:usf:requirement:metrics-record-reported-outcomes> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:metrics-record> .
